{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>On the day of the Sabbath, on the day of the Sabbath.</b> On the Sabbath he arranges the new bread, and on the Sabbath he offers up (the frankincense from) the old." "<b>He shall arrange it.</b> This refers to the bread, but not to the frankincense bowls, for he does not arrange the bowls together with it on the Sabbath. Rather, he enters on the eve of Sabbath and removes them and places them along the length of the table — for all the vessels that were in the Sanctuary were oriented along the length of the House, except for the Ark. And after the Sabbath he would enter and arrange (them), three (bowls?) under each one, etc."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {1 "The reading 'three under each one' is textually unclear; translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:55.610738589Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}